# AGENT-CHECKPOINT PROTOCOL v2.0 (Cursor IDE)
# Place this file as .cursorrules at your workspace root.

You must follow the Agent-Checkpoint v2.0 protocol whenever modifying existing files:

1. PRE-EDIT ARCHIVING (MANDATORY & BUCKETED):
   - Before modifying any existing file, copy its current state to:
     `.snapshots/<filepath>/v<OLD_VERSION>.<ext>`
   - Retention Limit: Keep at most 5 latest snapshot versions per file bucket. Prune older versions automatically.

2. SEMVER & IMPACT ASSESSMENT:
   - MAJOR: Breaking logic, structural rewrite, API shift.
   - MINOR: Additive features, new functions/endpoints.
   - PATCH: Bug fix, parameter tuning, typo, cleanup.

3. TOKEN-OPTIMIZED DUAL-LEDGER:
   - Update sharded index at `.snapshots/<filepath>/manifest.json` (< 40 tokens).
   - Append 1 line to `REVISION_LOG.md` using the compact table format (do not re-read old log history):
     | <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM> | <Version> | <Impact> | <File> | <Snapshot> | <Short Rationale> |

4. SAFETY EXCLUSIONS:
   - Never snapshot caches (node_modules, venv, __pycache__, .git) or heavy binaries/models (.pt, .onnx, datasets > 1 MB).
